 """Clocks the limiters read time from.
 
-Limiters never look at the system clock themselves: they call ``now()`` on the
-clock they were given, which returns seconds as a float. ManualClock is the
-clock for simulations and tests.
+Limiters never look at the system clock themselves: they call ``monotonic()``
+on the clock they were given, which returns seconds as a float. That makes the
+``time`` module a clock as it stands; ManualClock is the clock for simulations
+and tests.
 """
 
 
